WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.422 --> 00:00:05.371
- Oh (bleep) I can't with this sauce.

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.871
(light music)

00:00:10.945 --> 00:00:13.407
- Hey guys I'm Matt, a
producer here at Tasty.

00:00:13.407 --> 00:00:16.153
And today, I'm going to be
making a ton of tomato sauce.

00:00:16.153 --> 00:00:18.099
I wanna see what's
better, sauce from a jar,

00:00:18.099 --> 00:00:20.323
or two kinds of homemade tomato sauce.

00:00:20.323 --> 00:00:22.222
So I'm going to prep my
station, and get started.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.722
(light music)

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.820
There are tons of different
types of tomato sauce

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.326
available at the grocery store,

00:00:29.326 --> 00:00:31.035
but for this test I
opted for a traditional

00:00:31.035 --> 00:00:32.892
style sauce for it's simplicity.

00:00:32.892 --> 00:00:34.850
Just pour it out, heat
it up, and you're done.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.611
Idea for when you need a
sauce in less than 10 minutes.

00:00:37.611 --> 00:00:40.111
(light music)

00:00:43.772 --> 00:00:44.657
- What I notice right off the bat

00:00:44.657 --> 00:00:46.366
is that it's super sugary tasting.

00:00:46.366 --> 00:00:48.866
- It taste like dessert pasta.

00:00:50.637 --> 00:00:51.943
- Not into it.

00:00:51.943 --> 00:00:54.443
(light music)

00:00:55.293 --> 00:00:57.134
- [Matt] This homemade
tomato sauce is very easy,

00:00:57.134 --> 00:00:59.133
and can be prepared in under 30 minutes.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:00.449
The great thing about
making your own sauce

00:01:00.449 --> 00:01:02.079
is the huge amount of control you have

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:05.031
over the texture and flavor
versus with the jarred stuff,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.691
you just get what you get.

00:01:07.691 --> 00:01:09.339
With this homemade version, you can used

00:01:09.339 --> 00:01:11.137
crushed tomatoes to make
it as chunky as you want,

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.404
or blend it to make it
as smooth as you please.

00:01:13.404 --> 00:01:15.904
(light music)

00:01:20.027 --> 00:01:21.227
Yes making homemade tomato sauce

00:01:21.227 --> 00:01:22.985
isn't as inexpensive or as simple as

00:01:22.985 --> 00:01:25.136
pouring it out of a jar,
but the extra effort

00:01:25.136 --> 00:01:27.362
rewards you with something
much more flavorful,

00:01:27.362 --> 00:01:29.329
and satisfying.

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:31.829
(light music)

00:01:33.118 --> 00:01:34.759
- It has much more interesting flavors,

00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:36.071
it's much more savory.

00:01:36.071 --> 00:01:37.620
- Much more tomato in that one.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.696
- I like that it's more
chunky than the other one.

00:01:39.696 --> 00:01:42.157
I'm really into this (laughs).

00:01:42.157 --> 00:01:44.657
(Jazzy music)

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:47.822
- [Matt] If you have lots of time,

00:01:47.822 --> 00:01:49.895
and want a really fresh
tasting nuanced sauce,

00:01:49.895 --> 00:01:51.491
low and slow is the way to go.

00:01:51.491 --> 00:01:53.264
There's tons of methods
for making a slow simmered

00:01:53.264 --> 00:01:55.468
classic tomato sauce so
you have plenty of room

00:01:55.468 --> 00:01:58.639
for creativity and flexibility.

00:01:58.639 --> 00:02:00.551
Whole tomatoes give you a
fresher, brighter flavor

00:02:00.551 --> 00:02:01.705
than crushed ones.

00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:03.789
It's a bit more work to
crush the tomatoes by hand,

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:06.375
but it will help them cook down quicker.

00:02:06.375 --> 00:02:07.705
You can use carrots and celery in addition

00:02:07.705 --> 00:02:11.955
to the onion if you want
more flavor and sweetness.

00:02:13.524 --> 00:02:15.245
The longer you simmer,
the thicker and richer

00:02:15.245 --> 00:02:17.078
the sauce will become.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.640
If you really love the
flavorful punch of onions

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.890
and garlic, feel free to leave them in.

00:02:26.122 --> 00:02:28.037
A food mill is a good
way to filter out seeds

00:02:28.037 --> 00:02:30.166
and skin while giving
you a consistently smooth

00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:34.337
and glossy texture, you can
also use an immersion blender.

00:02:34.337 --> 00:02:36.837
(jazzy music)

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:47.967
From here, the longer it simmers for,

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.470
the better the sauce will get.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:50.808
Some people will let their sauce

00:02:50.808 --> 00:02:53.141
simmer for 12 hours or more.

00:02:54.312 --> 00:02:56.984
Add the fresh basil as close
to the end as possible,

00:02:56.984 --> 00:03:01.234
as it can lose it's flavor
the longer it cooks for.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.132
Yes, it takes much longer than both

00:03:04.132 --> 00:03:06.294
the jarred and 30 minute
sauce, but you end up

00:03:06.294 --> 00:03:09.794
with a much fresher, silkier tomato sauce.

00:03:14.769 --> 00:03:17.015
- Mmmmmmmmm, mhmmmm.

00:03:17.015 --> 00:03:18.384
- See that just takes like home.

00:03:18.384 --> 00:03:20.041
- The flavor feels more layered.

00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:22.567
- I feel like you should put this in a jar

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:25.296
and sell that on the shelf,
because this is bomb.

00:03:25.296 --> 00:03:27.796
(light music)

00:03:31.195 --> 00:03:33.110
- [Matt] When it comes to
price, the jarred sauce is the

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:36.452
most affordable, but barely
beats the 30 minute sauce.

00:03:36.452 --> 00:03:38.154
The jarred is also the most efficient,

00:03:38.154 --> 00:03:40.466
taking a fraction of the
time than the others.

00:03:40.466 --> 00:03:42.203
The homemade sauces offer
the greatest ability

00:03:42.203 --> 00:03:44.969
to customize both their
flavors, and textures,

00:03:44.969 --> 00:03:47.914
but the most important
question is, how do they taste?

00:03:47.914 --> 00:03:49.181
When put to the test my co workers

00:03:49.181 --> 00:03:51.515
overwhelming chose the homemade sauces.

00:03:51.515 --> 00:03:53.826
They liked the 30 minutes
bold tomato-ey flavor,

00:03:53.826 --> 00:03:56.488
and the two and a half
hours depth and freshness.

00:03:56.488 --> 00:03:57.761
Ultimately, tomato sauce
is what you make of it.

00:03:57.761 --> 00:04:00.064
Whether you have 30 minutes, or all day,

00:04:00.064 --> 00:04:03.814
it's worth giving one
of these recipes a try.

00:04:05.196 --> 00:04:07.292
(can pops) ahhh there we go.

00:04:07.292 --> 00:04:09.792
(light music)

